.TH M4TEST 1
.SH NAME
m4test \- regression test for m4(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B m4test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I M4test
loads
.BR /p9/dis/m4.dis 's
in-process test seam,
.BR runstring(prog) ,
and checks a representative subset of the programs used to develop
.IR m4 (1)
against golden output:
.BR define / undefine ,
.BR $0 through
.BR $9 " and " $# ,
.BR ifdef ,
.B ifelse
including its chained-triplet form, the default quoting (including
nesting), and the default
.B #
comment convention. Every expected string was checked once against the
host's real
.IR m4 .
.PP
Prints one line per failure to standard error, a final
.IR N " passed, " N " failed"
summary to standard output, and exits with a non-nil status if
anything failed.
.SH SOURCE
.B /p9/cmd/m4test.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR m4 (1)
.SH BUGS
Runs
.I m4
in-process via its
.B runstring
seam, not as a spawned subprocess reading real files and standard
input/output \(em so it does not exercise
.IR m4 's
own
.BR init ,
argument parsing
.RB ( -e / -f ),
or file I/O
.RB ( include )
at all.
